$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(2,4,4-trimethyl-pentyl)-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinane (62.4 g,
0.198 moles) and diethyleneglycol (133 g) were charged to a three-neck
500mL flask under nitrogen. The solution was heated to 60°C followed by
the exothermic addition of hydrazine (26.4 g, 0.448 moles) and KOH (27.8
g, 0.421 moles). The reaction mixture was then heated to reflux (136°C).
Water from the mixture was collected in an addition funnel by opening the
valve on the pressure-equalizing arm and allowing the water to evaporate
and condense in the funnel. Thus the temperature slowly climbed to 200°C
over 5 hours. The mixture was cooled to ambient and diluted with water
and toluene. Under stirring, concentrated HCl acid (35 ml, 37%, 0.355
moles) was gradually added to neutralize the pH to ~5-6. The organic
phase was separated and stripped of volatiles at 160°C/5mmHg. The final
product was obtained in 89% yield (49.7 g).
1-(2,4,4-trimethyl-pentyl)-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinane 3f, yield
89% (49.7 g).
