$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-cyclohexyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinan-4-one (28.4 g, 0.106 moles)
and diethyleneglycol (140 g) were charged to a three-neck flask under
nitrogen. The solution was heated to 60°C followed by the exothermic
addition of hydrazine (37.8 g, 0.641 moles) and KOH (35 g, 0.530 moles).
The reaction mixture was then heated to reflux (136°C). Water from the
mixture was collected in an addition funnel by opening the valve on the
pressure-equalizing arm and allowing the water to evaporate and condense
in the funnel. Thus the temperature slowly climbed to 190°C over 3 hours.
The mixture was cooled to ambient and diluted with water and toluene.
Under stirring, concentrated HCl acid (48 ml, 37%, 0.487 moles) was
gradually added to neutralize the pH to ~5-6. The organic phase was
separated and stripped of volatiles at 60°C/5mmHg. The final product was
obtained in 86.7% yield (22.1 g).
1-cyclohexyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinane 3b, yield 86.7% (22.1 g).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phosphorinanes as Ligands for Palladium-Catalyzed Cross-Coupling
Chemistry
