$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure of Reduction of Hetarenoindanone to Hetarenoindene
Exemplified by the Synthesis of 5,8-
Dimethyl-5,6-dihydroindeno[2,1-b]indole (3b). A mixture of 1.04 g (0.0042
mol) of 5,8-dimethylindeno[2,1-b]indol-6(5H)-one 2b and 1.12 mL (0.0224
mol) of hydrazine monohydrate in 20 mL of diethylene glycol was stirred
at 80 °C for 1 h and then refluxed for 1 h. The resulting mixture was
cooled to room temperature, treated with a solution of 1.2 g (0.0214 mol)
of KOH in 5 mL of water, and refluxed for 2 h. The resulting mixture was
poured into 100 mL of water, and the precipitate was filtered off, washed
five times with 50 mL of water, and dried. The yield was 0.84 g (86%) of
a greenish solid. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 25 °C), δ: 7.88 (m, 1H); 7.55 (d, 1H J =
7.4 Hz); 7.36 (m, 1H); 7.26 (m, 3H); 7.18 (d, 1H J = 7.4 Hz); 3.77 (s,
3H); 3.64 (s, 2H); 2.44 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 25 °C), δ: 148.2, 142.4,
141.0, 137.5, 131.4, 127.4, 125.7, 121.8, 120.6, 119.8, 119.7, 119.1,
117.8, 109.7, 31.0, 29.9, 21.3. Anal. Calcd for C17H15N (%): 87.52 C;
6.48 H; 6.00 N. Found (%): 87.48 C; 6.49 H; 6.03 N. Mp: 142-143 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Wolff -Kishner reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Method for the Synthesis of Hetarenoindanones Based on
3-Arylhetarenes and Their Conversion into Hetarenoindenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kashulin, Igor A.; Nifant'ev, Ilya E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2004), 69(16), 5476-5479

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME95 STEP1
$RXN



