$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-Methylpyrrole-2-yl Acetic Acid (4). Hydrazine hydrate
(43.1 g, 0.862 mol) was added to 1-methylpyrrole-2-oxo-2-yl acetic acid 3
(80 g, 0.522 mol). To this reaction mixture was slowly added 20% KOH
solution (900 mL). It was slowly heated to reﬂux and stirred at same
temperature for 5 h. Thereafter, the reaction mixture was cooled to 30
°C. The pH of the mass was slowly adjusted to 2 with 50% HCl at below 30
°C. Subsequently, the reaction mixture was extracted with dichloromethane
(3 × 300 mL). The organic layer was washed with water, dried over sodium
sulphate, and evaporated to give 60 g of 4 (82.5% yield and 98% purity by
GC). 1-Methylpyrrole-2-yl Acetic Acid, yield 60 g, 82.5%. Mass (M + 1):
140; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.58 (t, J= 2.4 Hz, 1H), 6.07 (d, J= 3.4
Hz, 1H), 6.05 (d, J= 3.4 Hz, 1H), 3.62 (s, 2H), 3.57 (s, 3H).
