$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-isobutyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinan-4-one (52.0 g, 0.228 moles)
and diethyleneglycol (58 g) were charged to a three-neck 500mL flask
under nitrogen. The solution was heated to 60°C followed by the
exothermic addition of hydrazine (25.0 g, 0.499 moles) and KOH (13.1 g,
0.233 moles). The reaction mixture was then heated to reflux (125°C).
Water from the mixture was collected in an addition funnel by opening the
valve on the pressure-equalizing arm and allowing the water to evaporate
and condense in the funnel. Thus the temperature slowly climbed to 215°C
over 4 hours. The mixture was cooled to ambient and diluted with water
(100 g) and toluene (60 g). Under stirring, concentrated HCl acid (23 ml,
37%, 0.233 moles) was gradually added to neutralize the pH to ~5-6. The
organic phase was separated and stripped of volatiles at 100°C/5mmHg. The
final product was obtained in 82% yield (40.0 g) and appeared as a clear
light orange liquid. 1-isobutyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinane 3a,
yield 82% (40.0 g)
