$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-phenylethyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinan-4-one (52.0 g, 0.189
moles) and diethyleneglycol (102 g) were charged to a three-neck 500mL
flask under nitrogen. The solution was heated to 60°C followed by the
exothermic addition of hydrazine (19.2 g, 0.384 moles) and KOH (11.9 g,
0.212 moles). The reaction mixture was then heated to reflux (135°C).
Water from the mixture was collected in an addition funnel by opening the
valve on the pressure-equalizing arm and allowing the water to evaporate
and condense in the funnel. Thus the temperature slowly climbed to 215°C
over 3 hours. The mixture was cooled to ambient and diluted with water
(100 g) and toluene (60 g). Under stirring, concentrated HCl acid (21 ml,
37%, 0.213 moles) was gradually added to neutralize the pH to ~5-6. The
organic phase was separated and stripped of volatiles at 100°C/5mmHg. The
final product was obtained in 78% yield (38.4 g) and appeared as a clear
light orange liquid. 1-phenylethyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinane 3e,
yield 78% (38.4 g)
