$DATUM (2R,3S,5S,6S)-2-(benzyloxymethyl)-6-(2-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)ethyl)-5-methyltetrahydro-2
H-pyran-3-ol (13) To a solution of 12 (1.24 g, 3.03 mmol) in ethanol (40
mL) was added tosyl hydrazide (0.85 g, 4.56 mmol) and the solution was
stirred at room temperature for 3 h. The solution was then concentrated
in vacuum and chromatographed on a silica gel column (with 15 % ethyl
acetate / hexanes) to afford a gum like product (1.75 g). This gum was
dissolved in a mixture of solvents (methanol: tetrahydrofuran = 20 mL :
20 mL) and cooled to 0 °C. To this solution was added sodium
cyanoborohydride (0.13 g, 2.07 mmol) and a little methanol extract of pH
test paper (Hydrion pH 1-11) to form a light yellow solution. Hydrogen
chloride solution in absolute ethanol (1 M, 1.64 mL) was carefully added
at such a rate that the color of the solution remained yellow. After
addition of hydrochloric acid the solution was stirred 30 min at 0 °C and
15 min at room temperature. The solvent was removed in vacuum and the
residue was purified on a silica gel column (with 25 % ethyl acetate /
hexanes) to give 1.70 g colorless gum.To a solution of 12 (1.24 g, 3.03
mmol) in ethanol (40 mL) was added tosyl hydrazide (0.85 g, 4.56 mmol)
and the solution was stirred at room temperature for 3 h. The solution
was then concentrated in vacuum and chromatographed on a silica gel
column (with 15 % ethyl acetate / hexanes) to afford a gum like product
(1.75 g). This gum was dissolved in a mixture of solvents (methanol:
tetrahydrofuran = 20 mL : 20 mL) and cooled to 0 °C. To this solution was
added sodium cyanoborohydride (0.13 g, 2.07 mmol) and a little methanol
extract of pH test paper (Hydrion pH 1-11) to form a light yellow
solution. Hydrogen chloride solution in absolute ethanol (1 M, 1.64 mL)
was carefully added at such a rate that the color of the solution
remained yellow. After addition of hydrochloric acid the solution was
stirred 30 min at 0 °C and 15 min at room temperature. The solvent was
removed in vacuum and the residue was purified on a silica gel column
(with 25 % ethyl acetate / hexanes) to give 1.70 g colorless gum. The gum
again was dissolved in absolute ethanol (60 mL) and the mixture was
degassed with argon for 5 min. To the solution was added 10.72 g sodium
acetate trihydrate and then the mixture was further degassed for 5 min.
The temperature of the mixture was allowed to rise to 75 °C and
maintained for 1 h. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuum to
give a slurry, which was then mixed with ethyl acetate (100 mL) and water
(50 mL). Aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 50 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with brine and dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate and filtered. The filtrated was concentrated in vacuum and
chromatographed on silica gel column (with 10 % ethyl acetate / hexanes)
to afford 0.88 g thick oil (overall 76 %). [α]20 D - 26.0° (c 2.70,
chloroform); HRMS-ESI (m/z) [M+Na+]: calcd: 417. 2437, found: 417. 2441.
IR (neat) 3430, 2928, 2857, 1471, 1386, 1255, 1104, 835, 735 cm-1; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 7.33-7.26 (m, 5H), 4.57 (q, J = 12.0 Hz, 2H),
3.87-3.54 (m, 6H), 3.28 (m, 1H), 3.12 (s, 1H), 2.05-1.86 (m, 1H),
1.86-1.75 (m, 1H), 1.75-1.64 (m, 3H), 0.96 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 0.90 (s,
9H), 0.05 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 137.7, 128.3,
127.6, 127.6, 79.9, 75.8, 73.5, 71.9, 65. 5, 59.7, 39.4, 35.7, 32.4,
25.8, 18.2, 12.7, -5.3, -5.4.
