$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-hydroxydihydrocinnamic acid hydrazide (V). A mixture of 3.3 g (0.04
mol) of 60% hydrazine hydrate and 2.12 g (0.01 mol) of chloropyruvate Ia
was heated at reflux in 30 ml of methanol for 8 h. The solution was
cooled, the separated precipitate was filtered off, dried, and
recrystallized. Yield: 73%. mp 160-162°C (i-PrOH). IR spectrum, ν, cm-1:
3310 br.s, 3250-2500, 1650, 1625, 1550, 1470, 1380, 1220, 1065, 1010,
715. 1H NMR spectrum (250 MHz), δ, ppm: signals from the fragment CH2CH
appear as a ABX system δA 2.42, δB 2.45, δX 5.05, JavAB 14.02, JAX 8.967,
JBX 4.52 Hz; 4.27 br.s (2H, NH2 or H2O), 5.46-5.48 m (1H, OH), 7.31-7.42
m (5H, C6H5), 9.08 s (1H, HNCO). 13C {1H} NMR spectrum (22.63 MHz), δ,
ppm: 39.44 (CH2), 64.13 (CH), 126.79 (Cn), 127.24 and 128.02 (CO) or
(Cm), 142.38 (Cand), 169.68 (C═O). Found, %: C 59.10; H 6.97; N 15.84.
C9H12N2O2. Calculated, %: C 60.02; H 6.66; N 15.56.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
