$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (b) Wolff-Kishner reduction: A mixture of (a), 3.5 ml of hydrazine
(anhydrous), 1.83 g (32.6mmol) of sodium hydroxide and 20 ml of
diethylene glycol was refluxed for 2 hrs. The reflux condenser was
replaced by a distillation adapter and Liebig condenser, the temperature
was slowly raised to 200 °C and held for 6 hrs. A mixture of hydrazine
and water distills over. The mixture was cooled, diluted with 30 ml of
water, acidified to pH 1-2 with conc. HCl, and extracted with
dichloromethane. The combined organic phase were washed with H2O and
saturated NaCl solution, dried over K2CO3 and evaporated. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography (n-hexane/ CH2Cl2 = 1).
Colorless oil. Yield: 70 %. 1H-NMR(CDCl3, 270MHz, δ from TMS, ppm) δ =
0.83 - 1.65 (m, 12H, cyclohexane-CH2 , CH2, CH3), 1.71 - 1.77 (m, 3H,
Ar-CH2-CH3 ), 1.84 - 1.89 (m, 4H, cyclohexane-CH2 ), 2.39 - 2.44 (m, 1H,
cyclohexane-CH), 2.52 - 2.55 (t, J = 7.74, 2H, Ar-CH2 -CH3), 7.08 - 7.12
(t, J = 8.1, 4H, Ar-H). 13C-NMR (270 MHZ, CDCl3, δ from TMS, ppm) :
13.98, 14.16, 22.76, 24.62, 26.7, 32.97, 33.46, 33.66, 34.31, 34.37,
34.42, 44.09, 125.649, 128.599.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Wolff-Kishner reduction
