$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-cyclopentyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinan-4-one (59.3 g, 0.247
moles) and diethyleneglycol (83 g) were charged to a three-neck 500mL
flask under nitrogen. The solution was heated to 60°C followed by the
exothermic addition of hydrazine (25.3 g, 0.505 moles) and KOH (14.3 g,
0.254 moles). The reaction mixture was then heated to reflux (136°C).
Water from the mixture was collected in an addition funnel by opening the
valve on the pressure-equalizing arm and allowing the water to evaporate
and condense in the funnel. Thus the temperature slowly climbed to 220°C
over 4 hours. The mixture was cooled to ambient and diluted with water
(60 g) and toluene (60 g). Under stirring, concentrated HCl acid (25 ml,
37%, 0.254 moles) was gradually added to neutralize the pH to ~5-6. The
organic phase was separated and stripped of volatiles at 100°C/5mmHg. The
final product was obtained in 55% yield (30.5 g) and appeared as a yellow
solid that was easily melted upon heating.
1-cyclopentyl-2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-phosphorinane 3c., yield 55% (30.5 g)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phosphorinanes as Ligands for Palladium-Catalyzed Cross-Coupling
Chemistry
