$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A crystal of Sc(OTf)3 was added at 0 °C to a stirred solution of mixed
aldehyde 3 (329 mmg, 1.1 mmol, 1 equiv), and
N,N’-bis(tert-butyldimethylsilyl)hydrazine (346 mg, 1.3 mmol, 1.2 equiv)
were in dry dichloromethane (2 mL) under nitrogen. After stirring over
night, and complete consumption of the aldehyde as indicated by TLC, the
volatiles were removed under vacuum, and the residue treated under
nitrogen at room temperature with a preformed solution of potassium
t-butoxide (2.5 g, 22.3 mmol, 20 equiv) in dry DMSO (11 mL) and t-butanol
(0.2 mL). The resulting red mixture was heated the reaction to 80 °C for
10 h to give a black solution. After cooling to room temperature, the
reaction mixture was diluted with water (20 mL), and extracted with
hexane (2 x 30 mL). The extracts were dried (Na2SO4), concentrated, and
subjected to chromatography on silica gel (eluent: hexane) to give an
alkane 4 (120 mg, 38%) as an oil. 3-Ethyl-3-methyl-heptadecane 4. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.752 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 6H), 0.746 (s, 3H), 0.88 (t, J
= 7.5 Hz, 3H), 1.05-1.35 (m, 30H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.0, 14.2,
22.7, 23.4, 24.1, 29.4, 29.7, 30.8, 31.0, 32.0,34.9, 38.4; MS (EI) m/z
267, 253, 169, 141, 127, 113, 99, 85. Anal. Calcd. for C20H42: C, 85.02;
H, 14.98. Found: C, 85.24; H, 14.80.
